    "title": "MIC-MAQ plugin training images",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.8186508",
    "publication_date": "2023-07-26",
    "description": "<p>*MIC-MAQ plugin training images*</p>\n\n<p>We provide images to train segmentation on fluorescence and brightfield images.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>For fluorescence:</p>\n\n<p>- QIBC dataset for nuclei segmentation and quantification (https://zenodo.org/record/8014997). The 3 channels of each field of view are saved in independant files: C1 (protein of interest, spots detection), C2 (EdU for quantification), C3 (nuclei segmentation).</p>\n\n<p>- Cyto dataset for nuclei and cell segmentation. The two fields of view are saved in a single LIF file that contains Z stack.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>For Brightfield:</p>\n\n<p>- Yeast dataset for cell segmentation</p>",
